course: dictionary
lesson: 8798
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Sharpen is a doing word, and its meaning changes with the words around it. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Sharpen your pencil before the test» means make the point sharper.
explain: Teachers say «sharpen your maths skills». Here the skill is the thing that gets better, through practice. You are not making anything pointy. Swap in «make» and check: make your maths skills better still makes sense.
explain: «Staying calm helps you think; panic does not sharpen your focus.» Your focus cannot be pointy, so sharpen means make it clearer and stronger. Always ask: what does this word do to the thing in the sentence?
fact: Sharpen means to make an edge or point sharper, like a pencil or a knife.
fact: To sharpen a skill means to make it better by practice.
fact: When a picture, sound or feeling sharpens, it becomes clearer or stronger.
fact: «Small AI programs hide in everyday things, such as phone cameras that sharpen photos.» Here sharpen means make the photo clearer.
fact: Adults sharpen kitchen knives, and that is a safety job for grown-ups.
exercise: Some chimps were reported to sharpen sticks to hunt small animals. What does sharpen mean here? | Paint in bright colours | *Make the point sharper | Break into small pieces
exercise: «Teachers say, sharpen your maths skills.» What does sharpen mean in this sentence? | Hide your skills in a drawer | *Make your skills better by practising | Lose your skills
exercise: «Phone cameras sharpen photos.» What does sharpen mean in this sentence? | Delete the photo | *Make the photo clearer | Make the photo darker | Print the photo small
test: «Staying calm helps you think; panic does not sharpen your focus.» What does sharpen mean here? | Make your focus smaller | *Make your focus clearer and stronger | Hide your focus
test: Which sentence uses sharpen to mean make an edge sharper? | Chimps use chewed-leaf sponges | Phone cameras blur the backgrounds | Ask people who care about you, and really listen | *Grown-ups sharpen the kitchen knives, as a safety job
exam: Ali says sharpen always means to make a pencil pointy. Which is the best reply? | *Sharpen can also mean make a skill better or a picture clearer, so check the context | Ask a grown-up to say it in a different language | Sharpen means to go to sleep | Ali is right, it only ever means pointy
